    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6968" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">casso</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caso</span></b> ), avi, atum, 1, v. n., rare
		collat. form of quasso (only in Plautus), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to shake</i>, <i>waver</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ubi bacchabatur aula, cassabant cadi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Mil. 3, 2, 41</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">v. 37: capitibus cassantibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Bacch. 2, 3, 71</span></i>
			; cf. quasso, II.</div>
